 R←Test_SendEmail_60(stopFlag batchFlag);⎕IO;⎕ML;⎕TRAP;parms;rc;msg;log;text
⍝ A recipient refused by the server: nothing is sent, the transaction is reset with RSET,
⍝ and `log` holds the answers to RCPT TO and RSET
 ⎕IO←1 ⋄ ⎕ML←1
 ⎕TRAP←(999 'C' '. ⍝ Deliberate error')(0 'N')
 R←T._Failed

 ∆SERVER.Defaults
 ∆SERVER.Refuse←,⊂'nobody@example.com'
 parms←∆NewMail'Created by SMTP''s ',⊃⎕SI
 parms.CC←'jane.doe@example.com,nobody@example.com,joe@example.com'
 (rc msg log text)←∆Send parms
 ∆SERVER.Defaults
 →T.PassesIf 1=rc
 →T.PassesIf'550 5.1.1 No such user'≡msg
 →T.PassesIf'250 2.1.5 OK' '250 2.1.5 OK' '550 5.1.1 No such user' '250 2.0.0 OK'≡log
 →T.PassesIf(⊂'RSET')∊∆SERVER.Commands
 →T.PassesIf~(⊂'DATA')∊∆SERVER.Commands
 →T.PassesIf 0=≢∆SERVER.Messages

 R←T._OK
⍝Done
